{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":3697482,"ns":0,"title":"A series and B series","extract":"In metaphysics, the A series and the B series are two different descriptions of the temporal ordering relation among events. The two series differ principally in their use of tense to describe the temporal relation between events and the resulting ontological implications regarding time.","description":"Philosophical descriptions of the temporal ordering of events","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}